  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜た ほう が いい",
     "texto": [
      "To advise doing something: past verb + **ほう が いい です**: **かさ を もった ほう が いい です** (it's better to take an umbrella).",
      "It sounds kind because you're not giving an order."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜ない ほう が いい",
     "texto": [
      "To advise not doing something: ない form of the verb + **ほう が いい です**: **あまい もの を たべない ほう が いい です** (it's better not to eat sweets).",
      "With **ほう** «this option» is compared with the others and you say which is best."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜ので: because; since",
     "texto": [
      "**ので** introduces a cause in an explanatory, gentle way: **あめ が ふっている ので、 うち に いた ほう が いい です** (as it's raining, it's better to stay at home). With nouns and -na adjectives **なので** is used: **あした は やすみ なので、 ゆっくり できます** (tomorrow is a day off, so you can take it easy)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
